Station BMGS-bori-field, located in Bori Metropolis, consists of a six-layer subsurface profile. The resistivity sequence starts at 1005 ohm-m, increases to 3588 ohm-m in the second layer, and then decreases through the third layer (1358 ohm-m) to a minimum of 333 ohm-m at the fourth layer. Following this, resistivity increases significantly through the fifth layer (2950 ohm-m) to a peak of 5469 ohm-m in the sixth layer. 

Based on the provided resistivity values, the calculated VES curve notation is KQHA. Please be advised that the existing on-file classification of H-type is inconsistent with the interpreted layer model and does not accurately reflect the observed resistivity trends.

